Quoting  archmage84  <archmage84@live.com>:
>I figured the skill penalties are a bit annoying at lower-levels, but
>when you have +20 to hit from your XPlvl alone, it's not that much of
>a big deal, is it?

In the middle to late game it is impossible to miss and as such there is
no point in worrying about to-hit penalties at all. Even the monk's -20
for body armour can be overcome.

>I guess my point is that non-weapon skills seem to be the only ones
>worth advancing, considering that even a x2 multiplier from an
>artifact for the damage is an extra _four_ damage. Whoop de do.

First of all, you get the skill slots, and for many classes, where else
are you going to spend them?

Secondly, you're looking at it wrong. It's in the early game where
characters die, and it is there where monsters are challenging - and where
even a single extra point of damage is useful (and a bonus to hit can
actually do something).

Thirdly, the multishot bonuses for launcher skills are well worth having.
